      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], **the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by never loading it into the Hub process at all**. Instead:\n\n1. A **local secrets loader** reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. The key is **injected only into the environment of spawned child processes** (the Ingest agent and Query agent) immediately before they start\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** \u2014 it never holds the credential\n\nThis design prevents a compromised or misbehaving Hub process from leaking the API key simply by reading its own environment variables. The key exists only in the short-lived child process that actually uses it to call the Anthropic API.",
